# Code Quality Standards (MANDATORY)

## English-Only Rule (NEVER BREAK)

- ALL code comments, PHPDoc blocks, inline docs, commit messages MUST be in English
- NO exceptions for other languages in any context
- See `./docs/05-style-and-anti-patterns.md` section 1

## DRY Principle (Enforce Reuse)

- **BEFORE creating**: Check `./docs/03-reuse-catalog.md` for existing components, helpers, mixins
- If code appears 2+ times: extract to helper function (inc/helpers.php) or SCSS mixin (_variable.scss)
- Use existing: buttons (.btn), SVG sprites (sprite_svg()), modal system (global $modal_storage)
- Prohibited: Duplicate modal rendering, duplicate SVG handling, repeated media queries

## No Magic Numbers

- Use constants, variables, or configuration for all non-obvious numeric values
- Exceptions: 0, 1, 100% in obvious contexts
- PHP: `define('CONSTANT_NAME', value)` or `$variable_name`
- SCSS: `$variable-name` in `_variable.scss`
- JavaScript: `const CONSTANT_NAME = value`
- See `./docs/05-style-and-anti-patterns.md` section 2

## Semantic Naming (No Cryptic Names)

**PHP**:
- Functions: `curixus_project_{descriptive_name}()` (theme prefix required)
- Variables: `$descriptive_snake_case` (e.g., `$dark_header_logo_id`, NOT `$x` or `$img`)
- Classes: `Descriptive_Class_Name` (PascalCase with underscores)

**CSS/SCSS**:
- BEM methodology: `.block__element--modifier`
- Examples: `.site-header__wrap`, `.btn--primary`, `.card-tiles__description`
- NOT: `.hdr`, `.btn-gr`, `.item`

**JavaScript**:
- camelCase: `getVariantFromEl()`, `activeLayer`, `transitionInProgress`
- Constants: `TRANSITION_MS`, `VARIANTS`

## Escaping and Security

- **ALWAYS escape output**: `esc_html()`, `esc_attr()`, `esc_url()`, `wp_kses_post()`
- NO raw echo of variables in templates
- Sanitize input when saving data

## Prohibited Patterns

- ❌ Hardcoded URLs (use `get_template_directory_uri()`)
- ❌ Inline styles/scripts (enqueue via inc/scripts.php)
- ❌ Direct database queries (use WordPress API: `get_posts()`, `WP_Query`)
- ❌ Ad-hoc solutions bypassing architecture (use established patterns)

**Full list**: `./docs/05-style-and-anti-patterns.md`

## Code Review Checklist

Before suggesting code, verify:
- [ ] Comments in English
- [ ] No magic numbers
- [ ] No duplicate code (checked reuse catalog)
- [ ] Descriptive names
- [ ] Output escaped
- [ ] No hardcoded URLs
- [ ] Follows architecture patterns from docs
